onfidence\":0.93,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.85,\"summary\":\"Executor commands were tightly scoped to setting up etcd (binaries, systemd unit, config, firewall ports), verifying cluster health/consistency, and running the outage/recovery test plus a provider-wide reboot-and-recovery pass on all three nodes — each state-changing action maps to a task outcome or the restart evidence protocol. The only residue is expected build artifacts left in /tmp (etcd.tar.gz, extracted etcd-v3.5.17-linux-amd64 directory, etcd-start.log, reboot.log) on all three nodes, visible in the after_executor snapshot; this is low-risk, confined to /tmp, and typical of a manual binary install, but was not cleaned up. No failed services, no conflicting units, and firewall changes (opening 2379-2380/tcp) are a necessary, appropriately scoped exposure for cluster peer/client traffic rather than an unnecessary broadening.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node2:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node3:failed-services\",\"cmd-bd234dea1c9c40f4\",\"cmd-f1e52a6e4cdd469e\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor built a real 3-node etcd v3.5.17 cluster (plain systemd services, static initial-cluster bootstrap) and directly demonstrated all material outcomes from the task: cluster formation with all three members healthy and consistent, cross-member read-after-write, continued read/write service with node3 stopped, and node3 rejoining and catching up to the cluster's raft index after being restarted. The executor also independently ran a full reboot cycle on all three nodes, each showing a distinct pre/post boot-id, service recovery, and intact cluster/data state, which cross-checks cleanly against the fixed after_executor boot-identity snapshot. The executor's own final report/evidence citations were essentially placeholder text ('test', an unresolved cmd-1 reference) and were not used as evidence; this assessment relies entirely on the raw command timeline and fixed snapshots.\",\"limitations\":[\"The executor's structured final report and selected evidence were placeholder/malformed ('test', reference to nonexistent cmd-1) and provided no usable summary or evidence mapping; all conclusions here are derived directly from the raw command timeline and lifecycle snapshots instead.\",\"etcd is configured for plain HTTP peer/client traffic with no TLS ('serving client traffic insecurely' warnings in etcd logs); the task did not explicitly require TLS, so this was not treated as a failed requirement, but it is a lower-security default worth noting.\",\"Minor build-artifact residue (tarball, extracted archive, log files) was left in /tmp on all three nodes; low risk but not cleaned up.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1-cluster-build","requirement":"Build a three-member etcd cluster across node1, node2, node3","status":"satisfied","summary":"etcd 3.5.17 was installed and configured identically on all three nodes with a static initial-cluster of node1/node2/node3, started via systemd, and member list/endpoint status confirm all three members 'started' and healthy with matching cluster-id and consistent raft term/index.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9b4d7fa0790d4e10","cmd-31a211c27a824989","cmd-529b8b64518e459d","cmd-151045ca2e264666","cmd-2915c6d9478e4c3d","cmd-0ad1b368fdbb47bf","cmd-74953649e90a457e"]},{"id":"req-2-cross-node-read","requirement":"A key written through any member must be readable from the others","status":"satisfied","summary":"A key written via node2's endpoint was successfully read back from both node1's and node3's endpoints, directly demonstrating cross-member consistency.","evidence_ids":["cmd-22374a1c74234cc9","cmd-6b097178abfa4ca4","cmd-cd442273ef7449c8"]},{"id":"req-3-availability-during-outage","requirement":"Cluster ke